PARTITION_NAME                           NOTES
---------------------------------------- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
P2020
P2021
P2022
P2023
P2024

========================================
We can gather partition-level statistics
over a period of time if necessary  prompt creating synopses as we go.

If statistics are being gathered on
the table during this period of time (e.g. using auto stats),
you might need to adjust how this is done. For example,
you could change the table's GRANULARITY
preference to GLOBAL, allowing
partition-level statistics to be created/updated
using this piecemeal approach without interference.
If you use a acript to gather stats on the
relevant table, this will need to be changed during
the process.
========================================
SQL> -- Gather per-partition statistics only
SQL> DECLARE
  2    v_owner   VARCHAR2(128) := USER;          -- or set to your schema name
  3    v_table   VARCHAR2(128) := 'SALES_DATA';  -- target table
  4  BEGIN
  5    FOR p IN (
  6      SELECT partition_name
  7      FROM   all_tab_partitions
  8      WHERE  table_owner = v_owner
  9      AND    table_name  = v_table
 10      ORDER  BY partition_position
 11    )
 12    LOOP
 13      DBMS_STATS.GATHER_TABLE_STATS(
 14        ownname          => v_owner,
 15        tabname          => v_table,
 16        partname         => p.partition_name,
 17        estimate_percent => DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE,
 18        method_opt       => 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO',
 19        granularity      => 'PARTITION',   -- do not touch global/table stats
 20        cascade          => TRUE,          -- include indexes in this partition
 21        no_invalidate    => DBMS_STATS.AUTO_INVALIDATE
 22      );
 23    END LOOP;
 24  END;
 25  /

PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.

Elapsed: 00:00:08.85
